  "worked_solution": "The supremum of a function is the supremum of the range of the function.\n\nIn this case, the range of $f$ is $A=(-1,4].$\n\nTo find the supremum of a set $A,$ we must find the set containing **all** upper bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of upper bounds) and take the minimum of this set.\n\nSo, in our case, we have that\n\n- any number $y\\ge 4$ is an upper bound of $A,$\n\n- any number $y<4$ cannot be an upper bound of $A$ because $4,$ an element of $A,$ is greater than $y.$\n\nTherefore, $[4,\\infty )$ is the set of upper bounds of $A,$ and\n\n$$\n{sup}_{x\\in R}f(x)=sup(A)=min[4,\\infty )=4.\n$$",
